# Git Safety Rules

## Forbidden actions

- Force push to any branch: `git push --force` or `git push -f`
- Destructive reset: `git reset --hard` without explicit user confirmation
- Direct commits to `main` or `master`
- Revert commits authored by other contributors without explicit user request
- Delete remote branches without explicit user confirmation
- Skip hooks: `--no-verify`

## Required behaviors

- Work on feature branches only
- Review `git diff --staged` before every commit
- Conventional commit format: `<type>: <description>` (types: feat, fix, refactor, docs, test, chore)
- Commit messages in English
- One logical change per commit

## Branch naming

```
feat/<short-description>
fix/<short-description>
refactor/<short-description>
chore/<short-description>
```

## Before any push

- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] No secrets or credentials in diff
- [ ] Commit message follows conventional format
- [ ] Branch is not `main` or `master`
